1
00:00:00,208 --> 00:00:01,417
[KARA]
Hello, Noah?

2
00:00:01,418 --> 00:00:02,419
[NOAH]
It’s a go!

3
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:03,877
Kara!

4
00:00:03,878 --> 00:00:05,212
So many blessings!

5
00:00:05,213 --> 00:00:06,715
Isn’t the universe amazing?

6
00:00:06,756 --> 00:00:10,051
- It always knows the perfect timing...
- Don’t. You’re going to make me cry.

7
00:00:10,093 --> 00:00:12,052
- Thanks, Carol.
- I love you.

8
00:00:12,053 --> 00:00:13,221
[KARA]
Super thank you.

9
00:00:13,263 --> 00:00:14,556
- [CAROL SQUEALS]
- [PEARL] Isn’t it nice here, Mom?

10
00:00:14,597 --> 00:00:15,140
Of course.

11
00:00:15,141 --> 00:00:18,226
- We’re here to celebrate Kara.
- Yes!

12
00:00:18,309 --> 00:00:20,436
[WAITER] Sorry, we have a
private gathering tonight.

13
00:00:20,437 --> 00:00:21,438
[WAITER]
So we are closed.

14
00:00:21,479 --> 00:00:22,772
[SANTI] Seriously?
We came all the way here,

15
00:00:22,814 --> 00:00:23,982
now you’re
telling us to leave?

16
00:00:24,107 --> 00:00:25,775
Hi, there.
I’m Santi.

17
00:00:25,984 --> 00:00:27,068
Excuse me?

18
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:28,903
[SANTI] You’re lucky
I even gave you attention!

19
00:00:28,945 --> 00:00:30,739
- [SANTI] Huh?
- [HAN BIN] Hey! Stop!

20
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:31,698
Hey!

21
00:00:31,906 --> 00:00:33,282
[PEARL]
Sir Han!

22
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:35,285
[MUFFLED YELLING]

23
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:38,621
[JAO]
Kara!

24
00:00:38,663 --> 00:00:39,663
[KARA]
How’s Pearl?

25
00:00:39,664 --> 00:00:40,665
[JAO]
She’s okay.

26
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:41,708
How about you?

27
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:43,710
I thought I was okay.

28
00:00:43,752 --> 00:00:46,337
What happened back there
brought everything back.

29
00:00:46,379 --> 00:00:48,088
Thank you for earlier.

30
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:49,382
If it’s for you,

31
00:00:50,383 --> 00:00:51,718
I don’t mind getting hurt.

32
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:52,760
[PEARL CLEARS THROAT]

33
00:00:52,761 --> 00:00:55,722
[JAO] I know it's hard for you
to trust people, but I’m here now.

34
00:00:55,764 --> 00:00:57,348
I’m not going anywhere.

35
00:00:57,390 --> 00:00:58,892
I love you, Kara.

36
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:19,287
[BICYCLE BRAKES SQUEAK]

37
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:42,392
[JAO]
Beautiful.

38
00:01:42,393 --> 00:01:43,394
Like a painting.

39
00:01:45,605 --> 00:01:48,107
This is better
because it’s real.

40
00:01:49,192 --> 00:01:51,277
And it’s right in
front of our eyes.

41
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:57,283
4,800 hectares of mangroves.

42
00:01:57,617 --> 00:01:59,410
One of the biggest
in the world.

43
00:02:01,579 --> 00:02:02,956
[SIARGAONON]
Absolutely beautiful.

44
00:02:05,083 --> 00:02:08,211
And soon enough,
Cabitoonan will look like this too.

45
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:11,421
There’ll be a lot more
Ruths out there, right?

46
00:02:11,422 --> 00:02:12,423
- Yeah.
- [JAO AND KARA LAUGH]

47
00:02:12,465 --> 00:02:14,050
And you’ll help us plant them.

48
00:02:14,092 --> 00:02:15,093
Of course!

49
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:16,719
I already promised, didn't I?

50
00:02:22,183 --> 00:02:24,978
You know, there's an
old saying from our elders.

51
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:29,399
[JAO SPEAKS SIARGAONON]

52
00:02:30,817 --> 00:02:32,527
[JAO SPEAKS SIARGAONON]

53
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:36,447
[JAO SPEAKS SIARGAONON]

54
00:02:38,408 --> 00:02:39,617
[JAO SPEAKS SIARGAONON]

55
00:02:41,327 --> 00:02:42,829
[JAO SPEAKS SIARGAONON]

56
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:44,998
[JAO SPEAKS SIARGAONON]

57
00:02:48,835 --> 00:02:50,879
Two people in love

58
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:54,924
who watch the
sunrise together

59
00:02:56,801 --> 00:02:57,802
will…

60
00:02:59,178 --> 00:03:01,014
always find their way...

61
00:03:01,681 --> 00:03:03,349
back to each other

62
00:03:04,183 --> 00:03:08,897
like the waves
meeting the shore.

63
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,441
Exactly.

64
00:03:12,650 --> 00:03:14,360
It’s a beautiful story.

65
00:03:15,778 --> 00:03:17,780
And I believe in
beautiful things.

66
00:03:19,657 --> 00:03:21,868
[JAO] I have faith
in beautiful things.

67
00:03:27,916 --> 00:03:28,917
Me, too.

68
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,630
This is the point of life.

69
00:03:35,298 --> 00:03:37,967
Watching the sun rise with…

70
00:03:39,427 --> 00:03:41,012
…with the person you love.

71
00:03:53,775 --> 00:03:55,360
I love you, Jao.

72
00:03:59,864 --> 00:04:01,950
No matter what happens,

73
00:04:04,369 --> 00:04:06,579
no matter where
life takes us,

74
00:04:09,832 --> 00:04:11,417
always remember,

75
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:15,380
as long as the waves
find their way back to shore,

76
00:04:16,255 --> 00:04:17,966
I’ll always love you.

77
00:04:37,068 --> 00:04:41,572
[ALON BY JL]

78
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:06,031
- [PEARL] Oh! Good day, sir!
- Hello.

79
00:06:06,032 --> 00:06:07,325
- Checking in?
- Yes.

80
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:08,784
Do you have
a reservation?

81
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:10,787
Yes.
It’s under Carina Flores.

82
00:06:10,828 --> 00:06:13,414
She’s my friend.
She booked this place for me.

83
00:06:13,456 --> 00:06:14,457
Okay.

84
00:06:17,710 --> 00:06:19,796
[PEARL]
Oh. There you go.

85
00:06:19,837 --> 00:06:22,632
- One room under Carina Flores.
- [GUEST] Yeah.

86
00:06:22,673 --> 00:06:24,258
[PEARL]
Well, welcome to Katig, sir.

87
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:25,885
Let me guess...

88
00:06:26,135 --> 00:06:27,135
Korean.

89
00:06:27,136 --> 00:06:28,596
Yes.
Very good guess.

90
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:29,638
[PEARL GIGGLES]

91
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:33,935
Yes. Because the owner of this hotel,
my boss, he’s Korean, too.

92
00:06:33,976 --> 00:06:35,770
[GUEST]
Ah, wow. Fantastic.

93
00:06:35,812 --> 00:06:37,188
I’d love to meet him.

94
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:38,439
Where’s he?

95
00:06:38,648 --> 00:06:40,817
Oh, he’s going to be
here in a few minutes.

96
00:06:40,858 --> 00:06:42,860
But in the meantime,

97
00:06:42,902 --> 00:06:44,278
can I have your
passport, please?

98
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:45,530
[GUEST]
Yeah, sure.

99
00:06:46,531 --> 00:06:47,615
[PEARL SPEAKS KOREAN]
Thank you.

100
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:49,659
- [PEARL LAUGHS]
- [GUEST] Thank you.

101
00:06:56,916 --> 00:07:01,838
[WAVES CRASHING]

102
00:07:04,549 --> 00:07:06,759
[SIARGAONON]
Good morning, everyone!

103
00:07:06,801 --> 00:07:08,886
I’m Ariel,
your island bestie.

104
00:07:08,928 --> 00:07:12,889
While I was delivering
sarongs today,

105
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:17,603
I came across this booth
promoting mangrove protection.

106
00:07:17,645 --> 00:07:19,230
We’re here at...

107
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:22,274
Shield the Mangroves,
Official Protector.

108
00:07:22,275 --> 00:07:25,278
- Say hi to our ambassadors!
- Hello!

109
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:28,822
All proceeds will go to
mangrove conservation efforts.

110
00:07:28,823 --> 00:07:30,533
It's really a community effort!

111
00:07:30,575 --> 00:07:31,659
- Wow!
- Yes.

112
00:07:31,701 --> 00:07:33,995
- Okay, let’s sign up.
- Okay.

113
00:07:35,371 --> 00:07:37,165
- Okay.
- Thank you.

114
00:07:38,249 --> 00:07:42,294
[ARIEL] Even the official sign-up
already comes with a loot bag!

115
00:07:42,295 --> 00:07:43,588
Wow!

116
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:46,756
Huge thanks to our sponsors!

117
00:07:46,757 --> 00:07:49,468
Thank you,
Shield bath soap.

118
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:53,055
Sign up now,
island besties!

119
00:07:53,222 --> 00:07:55,641
Till our next vlog!
Bye!

120
00:07:56,392 --> 00:07:57,393
[ARIEL]
Oh...

121
00:07:57,435 --> 00:08:00,521
Ariel, thank you so much
for promoting this event.

122
00:08:00,563 --> 00:08:03,649
- We’re so grateful!
- Anytime. Anything for the island.

123
00:08:03,691 --> 00:08:04,984
- Yes.
- You should join, too.

124
00:08:05,026 --> 00:08:06,110
Of course I will!

125
00:08:06,152 --> 00:08:09,030
This Menthol Cool is my favorite.
It’s refreshing on the skin.

126
00:08:09,071 --> 00:08:11,072
- That one’s great.
- This one, too.

127
00:08:11,073 --> 00:08:13,783
- That, too. It’s nice.
- Menthol Cool’s great on the skin.

128
00:08:13,784 --> 00:08:15,785
- Smells good, too.
- This is Honey and Orange Blossom.

129
00:08:15,786 --> 00:08:16,828
- Yes.
- Sounds like it smells good.

130
00:08:16,829 --> 00:08:18,247
I’ll try that next time.

131
00:08:27,089 --> 00:08:29,175
[KOREAN]
Stop it already.

132
00:08:29,425 --> 00:08:31,636
The guy you sent is
trying to take me back!

133
00:08:31,802 --> 00:08:34,679
[HAN BIN’S SISTER] We respect
your decision to stay in the Philippines.

134
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:35,431
[HAN BIN SIGHS]

135
00:08:35,432 --> 00:08:36,682
Listen carefully.

136
00:08:37,225 --> 00:08:39,310
I’m satisfied living
here right now.

137
00:08:39,435 --> 00:08:40,937
I’m not going
back to Korea.

138
00:08:41,229 --> 00:08:42,480
So don’t call me.

139
00:08:42,730 --> 00:08:44,439
[HAN BIN’S SISTER]
But you have to come home.

140
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:46,442
Father is in the hospital.

141
00:08:46,692 --> 00:08:47,693
What?

142
00:08:49,528 --> 00:08:51,155
You’re saying
Dad’s in the hospital?

143
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:53,199
[HAN BIN’S SISTER]
He’s very, very sick.

144
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,201
[HAN BIN SIGHS]

145
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:56,661
How's Mom?

146
00:08:58,287 --> 00:09:00,665
[HAN BIN’S SISTER]
Come home, young brother.

147
00:09:10,007 --> 00:09:11,884
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

148
00:09:11,926 --> 00:09:12,927
[PEARL]
Sir!

149
00:09:13,302 --> 00:09:14,303
Sir Han.

150
00:09:15,179 --> 00:09:17,807
We have a Korean guest
and he wants to meet you.

151
00:09:18,641 --> 00:09:19,642
I know.

152
00:09:19,684 --> 00:09:20,685
Oh...

153
00:09:20,935 --> 00:09:22,436
You’re expecting Sir Won?

154
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:24,730
Whatever happens, Pearl,

155
00:09:25,648 --> 00:09:27,066
please know that...

156
00:09:27,441 --> 00:09:29,819
everything that I’ve
ever shown you was real.

157
00:09:32,029 --> 00:09:32,738
Uh...

158
00:09:32,863 --> 00:09:33,948
[PEARL LAUGHS]
What’s...

159
00:09:34,115 --> 00:09:35,449
What’s happening?

160
00:09:36,617 --> 00:09:39,620
Did something happen?
Do I need to know anything?

161
00:09:39,662 --> 00:09:42,164
There’s a lot of things
I need to tell you, but...

162
00:09:42,623 --> 00:09:44,834
I never found the
right opportunity.

163
00:09:45,293 --> 00:09:47,503
I thought there was
always another time, but...

164
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:49,546
nothing’s guaranteed
in life and…

165
00:09:49,547 --> 00:09:50,673
Sir Han.

166
00:09:51,716 --> 00:09:54,218
Can you just please
go straight to the point?

167
00:10:03,394 --> 00:10:04,687
I like you, Pearl.

168
00:10:06,439 --> 00:10:07,440
A lot.

169
00:10:09,692 --> 00:10:12,486
Since the first time
I laid my eyes on you.

170
00:10:15,865 --> 00:10:17,867
But you didn’t say anything.

171
00:10:21,245 --> 00:10:22,663
I have my reasons.

172
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:27,084
Kara’s right.

173
00:10:27,626 --> 00:10:29,045
You are crazy!

174
00:10:30,129 --> 00:10:33,632
No, I just didn’t want things
to be awkward between us.

175
00:10:33,674 --> 00:10:35,343
But you didn’t say anything!

176
00:10:37,511 --> 00:10:38,971
You deserve to know now.

177
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:45,936
I don’t know what to say.

178
00:10:48,189 --> 00:10:49,190
Pearl...

179
00:10:50,066 --> 00:10:52,568
I’m not expecting
anything in return.

180
00:10:53,152 --> 00:10:56,489
I want you to concentrate
on chasing your dreams.

181
00:10:58,115 --> 00:10:59,825
If we are
meant to be together,

182
00:11:00,993 --> 00:11:02,661
fate will find a way.

183
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:10,169
Wait, you’re confessing,
but why does it feel like you’re...

184
00:11:10,211 --> 00:11:11,295
[PEARL BREATHES DEEPLY]

185
00:11:11,337 --> 00:11:12,713
you’re saying goodbye?

186
00:11:13,339 --> 00:11:14,548
Maybe because...

187
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:17,385
you’ll be taking
your Masters abroad.

188
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:20,429
I won’t say goodbye.

189
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:23,224
I’ll see you again.

190
00:11:56,757 --> 00:12:02,221
So, a Korean guy
showed up at Katig Hotel,

191
00:12:03,472 --> 00:12:07,977
and that gave Han Bin
the courage to confess?

192
00:12:13,357 --> 00:12:14,358
But…

193
00:12:16,318 --> 00:12:18,112
he’s not asking you out?

194
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:24,243
[CAROL]
How does that work?

195
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:27,329
[CAROL]
He just...

196
00:12:28,873 --> 00:12:31,584
- dropped a bomb on you.
- Exactly, Mom!

197
00:12:32,126 --> 00:12:35,629
That’s it!
That's exactly how I feel!

198
00:12:35,671 --> 00:12:38,966
So what am I
supposed to think now?

199
00:12:39,508 --> 00:12:40,593
[CAROL]
Think?

200
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:42,011
Pearlita!

201
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:47,766
The real question is…

202
00:12:52,229 --> 00:12:55,983
how do you feel about him?

203
00:13:41,529 --> 00:13:45,783
I know you’re just pretending
to deliver sarongs at Katig

204
00:13:45,824 --> 00:13:48,117
so you can talk to Sir Han.

205
00:13:48,118 --> 00:13:49,328
Of course.

206
00:13:49,495 --> 00:13:52,289
I want to know if he’s
serious about you.

207
00:13:53,415 --> 00:13:55,793
You’re the confusing one.

208
00:13:55,834 --> 00:13:58,420
I've known for ages
that he likes you.

209
00:13:59,588 --> 00:14:01,590
So?
Does he have a chance?

210
00:14:03,008 --> 00:14:04,343
How would I know?

211
00:14:07,555 --> 00:14:08,556
Well...

212
00:14:08,681 --> 00:14:10,266
did you sleep
at all last night?

213
00:14:12,017 --> 00:14:14,728
How could I, Ariel?

214
00:14:14,895 --> 00:14:17,189
After everything
he told me?

215
00:14:18,274 --> 00:14:19,024
[PEARL SIGHS]

216
00:14:19,025 --> 00:14:24,238
Now I don’t even know how
to act when I see him at Katig.

217
00:14:24,738 --> 00:14:25,739
Hm...

218
00:14:26,699 --> 00:14:29,201
Did he ask if you like him?

219
00:14:29,952 --> 00:14:31,745
No.

220
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:34,957
That’s the weird part.

221
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:37,167
He said,
“I like you, Pearl.”

222
00:14:37,209 --> 00:14:38,002
Hm.

223
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:41,630
But the way he said it sounded
like he was saying goodbye.

224
00:14:41,839 --> 00:14:43,841
I couldn’t sleep
because of that.

225
00:14:44,383 --> 00:14:45,676
Hey, Tantan!

226
00:14:45,884 --> 00:14:47,595
- Tantan!
- [TANTAN] Hey, Pearl.

227
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:49,971
[TANTAN] I drove
Sir Han earlier today.

228
00:14:49,972 --> 00:14:53,684
He was with
your Korean guest.

229
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:55,560
Where?

230
00:14:55,561 --> 00:14:57,563
To the airport.
T​​hey’re flying back to Korea.

231
00:14:57,605 --> 00:14:59,023
- [ARIEL] Huh?
- Airport?

232
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:02,568
He didn’t even say goodbye?

233
00:15:03,027 --> 00:15:05,613
[TANTAN] He said there was
a family emergency in Korea.

234
00:15:05,821 --> 00:15:07,114
Uh...

235
00:15:07,156 --> 00:15:09,574
He left some reminders
to you via email.

236
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:10,784
Pearl, check it!

237
00:15:11,035 --> 00:15:12,536
Read the email.

238
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:16,332
What does it say?

239
00:15:16,915 --> 00:15:18,125
[PEARL BREATHES DEEPLY]

240
00:15:18,917 --> 00:15:21,337
His father is in the ICU.

241
00:15:21,879 --> 00:15:23,504
And he doesn't know

242
00:15:23,505 --> 00:15:25,132
when he’ll be back

243
00:15:25,966 --> 00:15:28,218
- or if he’ll come back at all.
- [TANTAN] Huh?

244
00:15:28,636 --> 00:15:29,928
My gosh.

245
00:15:30,429 --> 00:15:33,265
He said he’ll send
a new manager.

246
00:15:33,932 --> 00:15:35,141
A new manager?

247
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:38,520
Because he’s sure
I’m going to Switzerland.

248
00:15:44,818 --> 00:15:45,986
Sorry, Pearl.

249
00:15:48,072 --> 00:15:49,948
Sir Han really
is confusing.

250
00:16:05,923 --> 00:16:09,008
[ARIEL] We're here today
at Barangay Cabitoonan

251
00:16:09,009 --> 00:16:13,763
for the first day of our planting
ceremony for the mangrove reserve.

252
00:16:13,764 --> 00:16:15,390
You should plant the first one

253
00:16:15,391 --> 00:16:17,809
because this project wouldn’t
be possible without you.

254
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:19,435
Let Egay do it.
Egay.

255
00:16:19,436 --> 00:16:20,436
Why me?

256
00:16:20,437 --> 00:16:23,314
Because what we’re
doing here today is for you.

257
00:16:23,315 --> 00:16:24,982
For the children of Siargao.

258
00:16:24,983 --> 00:16:28,611
Team Mangroves forever!
[CROWD CHEERS]

259
00:16:28,612 --> 00:16:30,863
[CROWD CHANTING]
Team Mangroves! Team Mangroves!

260
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:32,366
[KARA]
Who did this?

261
00:16:32,408 --> 00:16:34,200
[KARA]
It’s really disturbing how

262
00:16:34,201 --> 00:16:37,412
these people see paradise
and only think of profit.

263
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:39,622
I’m sorry, okay?
I don’t mean to offend you.

264
00:16:39,623 --> 00:16:41,124
I’m not generalizing either.

265
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:42,751
- But surely there are...
- Wait, wait.

266
00:16:42,918 --> 00:16:44,377
[WOMAN]
Kara, I'm sorry.

267
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:45,920
The Mayor won't be able
to meet with you today.

268
00:16:45,921 --> 00:16:47,422
But come back tomorrow.

269
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:48,799
Kara, look at this.
